          "text": "The dominant phase indexes as a **rutile-type tetragonal structure**, space group **P4\u2082/mnm (No. 136)**, with approximately:\n\n- \\(a = 4.737\\) \u00c5\n- \\(c = 3.173\\) \u00c5\n\nThe principal reflections are indexed as 110, 101, 200, 111, 210, 211, 220, 002, 310, 221, 112, 301, 311, 202, 400, 222, and 330. The O/F ratio is represented by occupational disorder on the rutile anion site: O = 1/6 and F = 5/6. Cu X-ray powder data cannot reliably distinguish a particular microscopic O/F ordering because O and F have very similar scattering factors. Several sub-percent weak features are therefore best attributed to short-range O/F ordering, a weak superstructure, or a minor impurity rather than used to select an arbitrary ordered model.\n\n```cif\ndata_Co3OF5_rutile_average\n_audit_creation_method              'Indexed and fitted from supplied Cu Kalpha1 powder pattern'\n_chemical_name_common               'cobalt oxyfluoride, rutile-type average structure'\n_chemical_formula_structural        'Co3OF5'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'Co3 F5 O'\n_cell_formula_units_Z               0.666667\n\n_diffrn_radiation_probe             x-ray\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength        1.5406\n\n_space_group_crystal_system         tetragonal\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt           'P 42/m n m'\n_space_group_IT_number              136\n\n_cell_length_a                      4.7372\n_cell_length_b                      4.7372\n_cell_length_c                      3.1728\n_cell_angle_alpha                   90\n_cell_angle_beta                    90\n_cell_angle_gamma                   90\n_cell_volume                        71.20\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1  'x,y,z'\n2  '-x,-y,z'\n3  '-y+1/2,x+1/2,z+1/2'\n4  'y+1/2,-x+1/2,z+1/2'\n5  '-x+1/2,y+1/2,-z+1/2'\n6  'x+1/2,-y+1/2,-z+1/2'\n7  'y,x,-z'\n8  '-y,-x,-z'\n\nloop_\n_atom_type_symbol\n_atom_type_oxidation_number\nCo  2.333333\nO  -2\nF  -1\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_ato